cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "dedekind"
abstract: >
  A C++23 library in which mathematical structure is stated as concepts and
  laws are constexpr values of the operations they are about, read by the
  compiler at compile time and by ordinary calls at run time.  The code keeps
  to three rules, the Juliet Posture: values are copyable data and functions
  are pure and constexpr; generic code varies with a type only through that
  type's concepts and traits; recursion only folds, over a term, a finite
  carrier or an explicit budget.  A checker in tools/jlt-check holds the core
  of the library to the rules in continuous integration.  Sets are arrows into
  a truth object, and membership and quantifiers over finite ordered carriers
  are decided by folds.
authors:
  - family-names: "Kräutler"
    given-names: "Vincent"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vincentk/dedekind"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - C++23
  - concepts
  - type classes
  - System F
  - parametricity
  - structural recursion
  - compile-time programming
  - category theory
  - lattices
  - intensional sets
